---
code: carry-netns-on-net-kernel-forbidden
when-fires: a kind's per-netns `net-kernel` store claims `invariant:netns` (a contradiction). oracle/carry.rs lift. `{kind_munged}` = the munged kind.
why: 27C §4(a): network kernel state is namespaced; the false invariance line is dropped.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- carry-netns-on-net-kernel-forbidden && mise run loom:promote -- carry-netns-on-net-kernel-forbidden`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all carry-netns-on-net-kernel-forbidden` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# The store is network kernel state, which every namespace holds its own copy of -- so the
# invariance line below cannot be true of it.
sm_dorc_Route__state_stored_only_in() {
   printf '%s\n' "$1" : stored-in net-kernel
   : undivided-by-transit-across netns
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
